// Armour and clothing shapes. Layers (outside in): cover, armour, over, under (plan §2.6). Coverage is 0-1 per body part.
// Layer sizes/permits and thicknesses are estimates; DF size multipliers (mail shirt 0.225, breastplate 0.2, helm 0.3,
// gauntlets 0.25) come from the Material science page. The clothing-only shapes (braies, hose, hood, coif, gloves, mittens, boots, shoes,
// leather jerkin, fur coat, oiled cloak, bedroll) live in clothing/garments.jsonc; resolver v2 reads both files as the worn layers.
// v2 (resolver-v2 3.2): blunt_absorb_pm is the share of momentum a crushed piece soaks up (padding: gambeson 450, padded coif 300;
// mail and plate 0); "visor": a closed visor leaves no face gap. 42 armour shapes in all, plus 4 shields in shields.jsonc.
